<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1973</h1><p class="ref-lede">1973 in world history: 26 events, 18 deaths, 2 states founded and 3 that came to an end. 223 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1969">1969</a><a href="/years/1970">1970</a><a href="/years/1971">1971</a><a href="/years/1972">1972</a><a href="/years/1973" aria-current="page">1973</a><a href="/years/1974">1974</a><a href="/years/1975">1975</a><a href="/years/1976">1976</a><a href="/years/1977">1977</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-15">15 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Nixon suspends offensive action against North Vietnam</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Citing progress in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> peace talks, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-nixon">Richard Nixon</a> halted US bombing and mining of North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris-peace-accords">Paris Peace Accords</a>, signed twelve days later, ended direct American involvement in the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-22">22 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US Supreme Court decides Roe v. Wade</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">By seven votes to two, the Court ruled that the constitutional right to privacy protected a woman's decision to have an abortion. The ruling was overturned in 2022.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-29">29 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Last US combat troops leave South Vietnam</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The final American combat units departed under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris-peace-accords">Paris Peace Accords</a>, and the last prisoners of war were released. Some 58,000 Americans and millions of Vietnamese had died in the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pablo-picasso" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pablo-picasso.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-8">8 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Pablo Picasso dies at Mougins aged 91</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pablo-picasso">Pablo Picasso</a> died at his home in the south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Co-founder of Cubism and creator of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guernica">Guernica</a>, he had reshaped modern art over a career lasting more than seventy years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pablo-picasso">Pablo Picasso</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-14">14 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">NASA launches Skylab, America's first space station</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Skylab was launched on the last Saturn V flown. Damaged on ascent, it was repaired by its first crew, and three crews lived aboard for a total of 171 days.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-17">17 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Senate Watergate hearings open on television</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Senate committee began televised hearings into the Watergate break-in and cover-up. Testimony revealed the White House taping system, which led to Nixon's resignation in August 1974.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-9">9 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Secretariat wins the Belmont by 31 lengths</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Secretariat set a world record for the distance and became the first US Triple Crown winner in 25 years. His Belmont time still stands as the race record.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-11">11 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Military coup overthrows Chile's President Allende</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Armed forces led by General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusto-pinochet">Augusto Pinochet</a> bombed the presidential palace, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador-allende">Salvador Allende</a> died inside. The US had worked to undermine Allende; Pinochet's dictatorship killed and disappeared thousands.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-20">20 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Billie Jean King beats Bobby Riggs in the 'Battle of the Sexes'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Before some 30,000 spectators in Houston and a huge TV audience, Billie Jean King beat former champion Bobby Riggs in straight sets. The match became a landmark for women's sport.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-6">6 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Egypt and Syria attack Israel on Yom Kippur</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Egyptian and Syrian forces launched surprise attacks on Israeli positions in Sinai and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golan-heights">Golan Heights</a> on the holiest day of the Jewish year. The war ended in Israeli counter-offensives and reshaped Middle Eastern diplomacy.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/athens" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/athens.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-17">17 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Greek troops crush the Athens Polytechnic uprising</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A tank broke through the gates of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> Polytechnic, ending a student occupation against the military junta. Dozens were killed, and the junta fell the following summer.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris-peace-accords" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris-peace-accords.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/paris-peace-accords">Paris Peace Accords</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Paris Peace Accords were signed on 27 January 1973 by the United States, North Vietnam, South Vietnam and the Viet Cong's Provisional Revolutionary Government, after years of negotiation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/kesavananda-bharati-v-state-of-kerala">Kesavananda Bharati v. State of Kerala</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Kesavananda Bharati v. State of Kerala was a case decided by a thirteen-judge bench of the Supreme Court of India in April 1973.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/yom-kippur-war">Yom Kippur War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Yom Kippur War was the surprise offensive of October 1973 in which Egypt and Syria sought to recover the lands lost in 1967, crossing the Suez Canal and storming the Golan Heights on the Day of Atonement.</p></div></li></ol></section>
