<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-chile"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Chile.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Chile</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Augusto Pinochet’s coup overthrows Salvador Allende on 11 September</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/new-zealand"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/New%20Zealand.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>New Zealand</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Britain joins the EEC, ending New Zealand's secure British market</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-greece"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Greece.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Greece</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The junta abolishes the monarchy</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/united-kingdom"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/United%20Kingdom.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>United Kingdom</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The UK joins the European Economic Community</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/swazi-kingdom"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Swazi%20Kingdom.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Swazi Kingdom</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sobhuza II repeals the constitution and bans political parties</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/tanzania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tanzania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tanzania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Dodoma is designated the future capital</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/language/arabic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Arabic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Arabic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Arabic becomes an official language of the United Nations</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/norse-religion"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Norse%20religion.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Norse religion</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Iceland recognises the modern Ásatrú fellowship as a religion</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/dictatorship"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dictatorship.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dictatorship</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">General Augusto Pinochet’s coup overthrows Chile’s elected government</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/military-junta"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Military%20junta.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Military junta</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The commanders of Chile’s army, navy, air force and police seize power and rule as a junta until 1990</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/presidential-democracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Presidential%20democracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Presidential democracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Chile’s armed forces overthrow President Salvador Allende, ending four decades of constitutional rule</span></li></ul></section>
